 <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
 <div class="bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-500 rounded-r-xl p-6 mb-8">
 <p class="text-badge font-black text-brandOrange uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">KEY TAKEAWAYS</p>
 <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed text-sm mb-4 speakable">Wireless charger sourcing in China splits into two supplier classes: factories that hold a WPC membership and publish measured coil data, and factories that print "Qi2 compatible" on a catalog. Only the first class can give you a Qi-ID that resolves in the public registry. The five numbers below, plus one thermal load test you run yourself, separate them in under a week.</p>
 <ul class="text-sm text-slate-700 space-y-2 list-disc pl-5">
 <li><strong>MOQ follows design ownership, not order size.</strong> In-stock ODM with laser logo starts at 500 units, a platform redesign at 1,000-2,000 units, and a full OEM build with a new mold at 3,000+. Asking for "your MOQ" without specifying who owns the drawing gets you a number that will change later.</li>
 <li><strong>The Qi2 certification adder is 1.20-2.00 USD per unit</strong> — a WPC-authorized authentication IC at 0.80-1.50 USD plus the per-unit royalty. A quote that undercuts the market by 3 USD is not "Qi2 certified"; it is Qi2-compatible hardware that cannot legally carry the trademark.</li>
 <li><strong>Five measurements catch a weak coil before tooling:</strong> Tx inductance 10.0 &micro;H &plusmn;5% at 100 kHz, Q-factor above 80, DCR 95 m&Omega; &plusmn;8%, ferrite &mu;i around 2,300, and FOD response under 180 ms.</li>
 <li><strong>FOB Shenzhen at 500 units:</strong> Qi2 15W magnetic pad 6.50-9.00 USD, 3-in-1 foldable station 12.00-16.00 USD, magnetic car mount 8.00-12.00 USD, desktop stand 7.00-10.00 USD. Prices fall 40-45% at 5,000 units.</li>
 <li><strong>Shenzhen, Dongguan and Guangzhou are not interchangeable.</strong> Shenzhen gives you coil and IC sourcing density plus fast NPI, Dongguan gives you mid-volume cost balance, Guangzhou gives you the lowest unit cost at high volume with the longest engineering queue.</li>
 </ul>
