<!-- FAQ -->
<section id="faq" class="mb-16">
 <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
 <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl p-8 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-8 text-center">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
 <div class="space-y-6 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">What is the MOQ for OEM wireless charger manufacturing in China?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">It depends on who owns the design. In-stock ODM with laser-engraved logo starts at 500 units. A platform redesign that keeps stock packaging starts at 1,000 units, and custom branded packaging or structural changes start at 2,000. A full OEM project using your own drawing with a new injection mold starts at 3,000 units and adds 2-3 months for tooling before mass production begins.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">What is the FOB Shenzhen price for Qi2 wireless chargers?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">At 500 units, a Qi2 15W magnetic pad runs 6.50-9.00 USD, a 3-in-1 foldable station 12.00-16.00 USD, a magnetic car mount 8.00-12.00 USD, and a desktop stand 7.00-10.00 USD. At 5,000 units those bands fall to 3.50-5.00, 7.00-11.00, 5.00-7.50 and 4.00-6.00 USD. All prices include the Qi2 authorization IC and WPC per-unit royalty and exclude freight, duty and certification fees.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">Which certifications must a wireless charger supplier provide?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Five documents matter for a Qi2 pad: WPC Qi certification with a Qi-ID that resolves in the public product registry, CE marking covering LVD and EMC, RoHS, FCC ID for the wireless transmitter rather than a generic SDoC, and IEC 62368-1 safety test reports. Expect 3,000-5,000 USD and 4-8 weeks for the WPC lab work per SKU, and 2,000-5,000 USD for the FCC ID. A supplier who sends only PDF certificates without database references has not been verified.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">How do I verify a wireless charger factory's Qi2 coil quality?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Ask for five measured parameters from a named batch: Tx coil inductance of 10.0 uH plus or minus 5 percent at 100 kHz, Q-factor above 80, DC resistance of 95 mOhm plus or minus 8 percent, ferrite initial permeability near 2,300 on an MnZn sheet, and foreign object detection response under 180 ms. Then run your own one-hour 15W load test. A pad whose case temperature rises more than 17.5 degrees C above a 25 degree room is losing efficiency in the coil rather than the silicon.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">How long does OEM wireless charger production take from sample to shipment?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">For an in-stock ODM model, samples ship in 3-7 days and mass production takes 25-35 days. A platform redesign adds 25-45 days of engineering before production, and mass production then runs 35-50 days. A full OEM build with a new mold needs 7-14 days for samples, 30-60 days of production, plus 2-3 months of tooling. Add 4-5 weeks of sea freight to Europe or North America if you ship by water.</p>
 </div>
 </div>
 </div>
 </div>
</section>

